# Frontend Standards

## CSS Modules (No Tailwind)

- All styles use CSS Modules — one `.module.css` file per component, colocated in the same folder
- CSS custom properties defined in `src/styles/tokens.css` — never hardcode colours, spacing, or font sizes
- Use `clsx` for conditional class composition

```tsx
// CharacterCard.tsx
import styles from './CharacterCard.module.css';
import clsx from 'clsx';

export function CharacterCard({ active }: CharacterCardProps) {
  return <div className={clsx(styles.card, active && styles.cardActive)} />;
}
```

```css
/* CharacterCard.module.css */
.card {
  padding: var(--space-4);
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
}
.cardActive {
  border: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
}
```

## Component Rules

- Functional components only — no class components
- One component per file; filename matches the exported component name
- Props type named `[ComponentName]Props`
- Colocate component, CSS module, and test in the same directory with a barrel `index.ts`

```
features/character/CharacterCard/
├── CharacterCard.tsx
├── CharacterCard.module.css
├── CharacterCard.test.tsx
└── index.ts
```

## State Management

- **TanStack Query** owns all server state — fetching, caching, mutations, invalidation
- **Zustand** for client-only UI state (initiative tracker, modal state, session UI)
- Never store server data in Zustand
- Query keys defined as constants in the service file

```typescript
// services/characters.ts
export const characterKeys = {
  all: ['characters'] as const,
  detail: (id: string) => ['characters', id] as const,
};
```

## Forms

- **React Hook Form** + **Zod resolver** for all forms
- Schema always imported from `packages/shared` — never define validation inline

## Real-Time (Socket.io)

- Socket client initialised once in `src/lib/socket.ts`
- Wrap listeners in custom hooks that clean up on unmount
- Never emit directly from components — go through service functions
- Event types imported from `packages/shared`
